"""brixx mirror: correct BRIXX's real Postgres-native column types

Revision ID: 0046
Revises: 0045
Create Date: 2026-11-15 20:53:44

0045 assumed BRIXX returns Oracle-style type names (NUMBER, VARCHAR), matching the doc examples and the
committed metadata_example/ fixture. The real API returns Postgres-native names instead (BIGINT, NUMERIC,
SMALLINT, INTEGER, UUID, BOOLEAN, BYTEA): sql_type() didn't recognize them, so ~44% of real columns
silently became TEXT -- including primary/foreign keys, which is what broke BRIXX document downloads
(brixx_documents.document_id BigInteger compared against brixx.prg_document.prg_documentid, wrongly Text).
Drops and recreates the whole brixx schema with the corrected types: safe, since it is a pure mirror with
no source-of-truth data -- BRIXX resyncs it from scratch on the next cron tick. Hand-assembled from the
same codegen primitives (plan_delta/render_migration) against an empty existing-mirror, not the plain
`codegen` CLI command, because that command refuses to touch an already-committed revision's tables; the
next real `codegen` run will treat this revision's BRIXX_MIRROR marker as its baseline as usual.

Do not edit: BRIXX changes get a new revision from the next codegen run, which reads BRIXX_MIRROR to emit the delta.
"""

from collections.abc import Sequence

import sqlalchemy as sa
from alembic import op
from sqlalchemy.dialects import postgresql

